# Holodex — local config (copy to .env; .env is gitignored). One file, two readers:
#   • `docker compose` substitutes ${MEDIA_PATH} into the read-only media bind-mount.
#   • the Go binary's config loader (ADR-027) reads these as env vars in local dev
#     (`go run ./cmd/holodex`) — so the same .env drives both workflows.
# Real environment variables and CLI flags still win (precedence: CLI > env > yaml > .env).

# Absolute host path to your video library — required to scan anything.
#   native Windows (`go run`, Docker Desktop):  E:/Videos
#   inside a WSL/Linux shell:                    /mnt/e/Videos  or  /srv/media
# Under compose this is the host bind-mount source (mounted at /media in the container);
# for `go run` it is the path the binary scans directly. Defaults to ./media if unset.
MEDIA_PATH=/path/to/your/videos

# --- Optional local-dev convenience (uncomment as needed) ---
# Loopback bind avoids the Windows Firewall "allow access" prompt each run; the Vite
# dev proxy still reaches the API at localhost:7800. (Compose ignores HOST.)
# HOST=127.0.0.1

# Gate the owner-only admin + enrichment controls. Set whenever the server is
# reachable beyond loopback; the owner enters it once in the UI (it is then
# exchanged for an HttpOnly session cookie — ADR-045 — so a reload stays signed in).
# ADMIN_TOKEN=change-me
# Optional: sign the session cookie with an independent key (default: derive from
# ADMIN_TOKEN, so rotating the token signs everyone out).
# SESSION_SECRET=change-me-too

# LOG_LEVEL=debug          # debug | info | warn | error
# DATA_PATH=./data         # read-write dir: db, thumbnails, config
